From b02e746c06a7ce1a81e00fbc9390e6059df2fb99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:15:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] coag: geometric-edge IC + re-run Part B; gate on
 continuous L1 only

Adopt bin-centered (geometric-mean-edge) exponential IC in exp_ic_bins, replacing
the [m_k,m_{k+1}) binning (brief 1d wording). The old convention put NEMO's IC off
by half a bin vs the bin centered on the representative mass m_k that the density
reconstruction and DustPy/analytic use -- a t0 offset that inflated NEMO's error
and, being largest at coarse resolution, manufactured disc-L1 monotonicity.

With the correct IC:
- continuous L1 (L&L Eq.40, integrated) stays cleanly monotone -> GATE:
    constant 0.421>0.249>0.174>0.131 ; additive 0.458>0.267>0.187>0.142
- discrete L1 (Eq.41) and L2 are point-evaluated and fragile in the sparse
  over-diffused tail (non-monotone at evolved times) -> reported as diagnostics,
  NOT gated (same reason L2 was dropped). continuous L1 is L&L's primary norm and
  the conservation-law norm the chemically relevant grain integrals resemble.

Part B figure + data TSVs regenerated. Additive commit on top of the pushed Part B
(no history rewrite).
